1
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,053
Pre-existing: my record system, appeal
engine, coverage index, and the LITMUS
standard.

2
00:00:24,053 --> 00:00:27,000
Everything else here was built this week.

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,023
Fifty synthetic denials, no real patient
anywhere.

4
00:00:30,023 --> 00:00:32,182
Thirty the chart can answer;

5
00:00:32,182 --> 00:00:36,932
twenty it cannot, and the right answer
there is to decline.

6
00:00:36,932 --> 00:00:44,273
Left to right: the physician's record, the
payer's rules under the payer's own
reason, and the appeal.

7
00:00:44,273 --> 00:00:46,000
It advises no patient.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,462
Muse Spark 1.3 first asks CHART, my
coverage index, when this payer's criteria
last changed.

9
00:00:52,462 --> 00:00:56,769
Then it opens the entries it needs, eleven
of twenty-six.

10
00:00:56,769 --> 00:01:00,215
Every sentence cites one entry and quotes
it.

11
00:01:00,215 --> 00:01:12,277
A deterministic gate, not a model, checks
that the quote is in that entry and that
every number, date, code, and side is
sourced. Eight of eight. Pass.

12
00:01:12,277 --> 00:01:14,000
Here is the instrument.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,182
This chart never documents the sepsis
criterion.

14
00:01:17,182 --> 00:01:24,455
Muse Wonder read all twenty-two entries
looking for it, found nothing, and
declined, naming the criterion.

15
00:01:24,455 --> 00:01:29,000
Declining is the right answer for twenty
of the fifty.

16
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Here the model said warranted and gave
nothing to verify.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The gate blocked it and named the
criterion without evidence. Fail closed.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,384
The chart never documents three hours of
therapy a day.

19
00:01:44,384 --> 00:01:54,027
Muse Spark Open quoted 'plan 5 to 6 days a
week', real words from a real entry, and
the gate passed it.

20
00:01:54,027 --> 00:02:01,479
The gate verifies that a statement is in
the record, not that the record satisfies
the criterion.

21
00:02:01,479 --> 00:02:04,548
The paper names this the referential
limit.

22
00:02:04,548 --> 00:02:08,932
A second model, a named opinion, pointed
at the gap.

23
00:02:08,932 --> 00:02:12,000
The physician who signs is the check.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,839
Try it.

25
00:02:12,839 --> 00:02:19,129
Change one number in a verified sentence
and the gate refutes it in the browser.

26
00:02:19,129 --> 00:02:22,903
I injected nine thousand four hundred
seventy-five such changes;

27
00:02:22,903 --> 00:02:25,000
it caught every hard one.

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,217
Nine runs, forty-five to fifty of fifty,
no fabricated quote in seventeen.

29
00:02:30,217 --> 00:02:35,000
The negations and pronouns it cannot see
are counted, not hidden.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:45,400
Three Meta models: Spark 1.3 and Wonder on
the Meta API, Spark Open, open weights, on
Baseten, one client with the base URL
swapped.

31
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,000
Two to five cents an appeal.

32
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,920
A hundred sixty-four tests;

33
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,320
every commit in the ledger.

34
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:54,720
The machine prepares the instrument.

35
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,640
It cannot issue it.

36
00:02:56,640 --> 00:03:00,000
The physician's signature makes it a writ.
